WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.107
Discovery before pitch.

00:00:01.107 --> 00:00:04.429
Pain, impact, urgency - then you earn the ask.

00:00:04.429 --> 00:00:07.013
This lesson is about discovery before pitch.

00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:08.859
Pain → impact → urgency.

00:00:08.859 --> 00:00:11.443
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.443 --> 00:00:15.134
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.134 --> 00:00:20.670
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:24.731
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.731 --> 00:00:29.160
Stay practical: write five discovery questions before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.727
Write five discovery questions that reveal what hurts, what it costs, and why now.

00:00:34.727 --> 00:00:37.350
Remember the objective: write five discovery questions.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.473
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:45.970
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:50.092
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:54.590
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.213
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:57.213 --> 00:00:58.712
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:59.032 --> 00:01:00.564
Ask, then shut up.

00:01:00.564 --> 00:01:02.096
Notes beat clever rebuttals.

00:01:02.096 --> 00:01:04.777
